  <p class="text-lg">
    A custom data acquisition system designed to capture, log, and analyze weld current
    waveforms in real time.
  </p>

  <h2>Overview</h2>
  <p>
    The system uses a microcontroller paired with a current sensor to capture high-frequency
    weld data during production. Alongside the electrical data, synchronized high-speed video
    was captured to visually document weld events. All captured data is transferred to a host
    machine for real-time monitoring and logging.
  </p>

  <p>
    A companion analysis tool provides waveform visualization, filtering, peak detection,
    and reporting capabilities to support weld quality assessment.
  </p>

